# Cloudflare Pages' default static-asset caching (4h for .js, matched by
# extension) meant a bug fix to js/scoring.js or js/api.js could sit
# invisible for up to 4 hours in any browser that had already cached the old
# copy — confirmed 2026-09: a scoring fix worked immediately in Safari
# private mode (empty cache) but not normal mode (still serving a cached
# pre-fix scoring.js, well within its 4h window, so it never even asked the
# server for a fresh copy). Force revalidation on every load instead — still
# cacheable, just never trusted without checking first.
#
# NOTE (2026-11-11): on the real domain (mashupgolf.com) a Cloudflare zone setting — Caching → Configuration →
# "Browser Cache TTL" — used to rewrite these to max-age=14400 (4h), so these rules did NOT protect real
# visitors (it caused a site-wide outage after a js/api.js change). It is now "Respect Existing Headers" and
# the rules below work on the real domain. If that setting is ever reverted they silently stop working again,
# so ALSO bump the `?v=` label on every js/css reference when a file changes (see CLAUDE.md "Cache-busting").
/js/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# Same reasoning for the shared stylesheet (css/theme.css) — a visual fix
# shouldn't sit behind a stale cached copy.
/css/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# Scorecards already got no-store at the fetch call itself (js/api.js), but
# set it here too as defense-in-depth against any cache layer that ignores
# fetch-level cache options.
/data/scorecards/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
